      'a FOUL BALL is a batted ball that settles in FOUL territory outside the first or third base lines before passing first or third base or that first lands in fair territory beyond the bases but then rolls foul without being touched or a fly caught in foul ground a foul ball is a DEAD ball runners cannot advance and it counts as a STRIKE unless the batter already has two strikes in which case it is simply replayed a foul TIP caught by the catcher is different it is a strike and stays live',
